# p23-required-names.txt.example — format rules ONLY (the real names file
# ships alongside; this file documents the format and never feeds a guard).
#
# Format:
#   - one top-level Go test name per line
#   - `#` starts a comment; blank lines are ignored
#   - duplicates collapse to the FIRST occurrence (distinct-name counting)
#   - a missing or empty (comments-only) names file makes `integration`
#     mode REFUSE to bless any run (fail closed — an empty guard must
#     never pass a run)
#
# Honesty rule: the header of the real file records whether each name has
# actually RUN+PASSed in a real log at pinning time. Synthetic selftest
# logs (selftest_guard_p23.sh) never count as execution evidence.
#
# Example line (NOT a real test — do not add to the real file):
# TestPGExampleNameOnly
